\section*{Key equations (hand-transcribed from the PDF)}

Chung, Yao, Hughes, Kim, ``Nature of a topological quantum phase transition in a
chiral spin liquid model,'' arXiv:0909.2655 (2009).

Majorana representation of the spin-1/2 operators (Kitaev/Yao-Kivelson), with
constraint:
\[ \sigma_i^\alpha = i\, c_i\, d_i^\alpha, \qquad
   D_i \equiv c_i\, d_i^x\, d_i^y\, d_i^z = 1 . \tag{1} \]

Majorana Hamiltonian on the star / decorated-honeycomb lattice, with static
$Z_2$ gauge fields $\hat u_{ij}=-i d_i^\alpha d_j^\alpha \to u_{ij}=\pm1$:
\[ H[\{\hat u_{ij}\}] = J \sum_{x,y,z\text{-link}} \hat u_{ij}\, i\, c_i c_j
   + J' \sum_{x',y',z'\text{-link}} \hat u_{ij}\, i\, c_i c_j . \tag{2} \]

Diagonalized quadratic form (6 sites/cell, band index $n=1,2,3$), with
$g\equiv J'/J$:
\[ H[\{u_{ij}\}] = J \sum_{n,\mathbf k} \epsilon_{n,\mathbf k}[\{u_{ij}\};g]
   \left(b^\dagger_{n,\mathbf k} b_{n,\mathbf k} - \tfrac12\right). \tag{3} \]

Uniform-flux ground state: $\phi^0_L=-1$ on all 12-plaquettes and
$\phi^0_L=\pm1$ on all triangles (spontaneously breaks time reversal). The
topological degeneracy changes across the nA$\to$A transition at
\[ g_c = \sqrt{3}. \]

Global $Z_2$ flux operators on the two torus cycles $\Gamma_x,\Gamma_y$:
\[ \Phi_\alpha \equiv \prod_{\langle ij\rangle\in\Gamma_\alpha} u_{ij} = \pm1,
   \qquad \alpha = x,y. \tag{4} \]

Finite-temperature global-flux expectation value:
\[ \langle \Phi_\alpha(T)\rangle \equiv \frac1Z \,\mathrm{tr}\,
   \Phi_\alpha e^{-H/T}, \tag{5} \]
\[ \langle \Phi_\alpha\rangle = \frac{\sum_{\Phi_x,\Phi_y=\pm1}
   \Phi_\alpha\, Z^{(\Phi_x,\Phi_y)}}{Z}. \tag{6} \]

Headline result — quantized $T=0$ global flux:
\[ \langle\Phi_x\rangle(T=0) =
   \begin{cases} 1/3 & \text{(nA, } g<g_c) \\ 0 & \text{(A, } g>g_c) \end{cases}. \tag{7} \]

Topological-degeneracy relation:
\[ n_{\mathrm{DEG}} = 4 - 3\langle\Phi_x\rangle(T=0). \tag{8} \]

Crossover-scale system-size dependence:
\[ T^* \sim \frac{\Delta(g)}{\ln N}. \tag{9} \]

Thermalized reduced density matrix (finite-$T$ entanglement entropy):
\[ \rho_A(T) = \sum_\lambda \frac{e^{-E_\lambda/T}}{Z}\,
   \mathrm{Tr}_B |\Phi_\lambda\rangle\langle\Phi_\lambda|. \tag{10} \]

Sub-partition-function combination in the nA sector (odd parity in $(-1,-1)$):
\[ Z^{(1,1)}_{\rm CSL} \pm Z^{(-1,-1)}_{\rm CSL} = 2\exp(-E_G/T). \tag{12} \]

Finite-$T$ global flux in terms of the fermion spectrum (used in this replication):
\[ \langle\Phi_x\rangle(T) =
   \frac{\prod_{n,\mathbf k}\tanh(\epsilon_{n,\mathbf k}/2T)}
        {2 + \prod_{n,\mathbf k}\tanh(\epsilon_{n,\mathbf k}/2T)}. \tag{13} \]

As $T\to0$, $\tanh\to1$ so $P\equiv\prod\tanh\to1$ and
$\langle\Phi_x\rangle\to 1/(2+1)=1/3$, recovering Eq.(7).

Bounds (SOM):
\[ \tfrac13\big[\tanh(\Delta/2T)\big]^N < \langle\Phi_x\rangle
   < \tfrac13\big[\tanh((\Delta+W)/2T)\big]^N. \]

Topological entanglement entropy (unchanged across the QPT):
\[ S_{\rm ent} = \alpha L - \gamma, \qquad
   \gamma = \ln\sqrt{\textstyle\sum_\alpha d_\alpha^2} = \tfrac12\ln 2 \ \text{(both phases)}. \]

