Thus there is only a three-fold topological ground state
degeneracy in the nA phase. In summary, for A phases
with uniform flux, all the physical states consist of an
even number of fermionic quasiparticle excitations above
the ground states in all four topological sectors. For nA
phases with uniform flux, all physical states have an even
number of fermion excitations in sectors (1, 1), (1, −1),
and (−1, 1), but an odd number of fermion excitations
in the sector (−1, −1). This has consequences not only
for the topological ground state degeneracy, but also at
finite temperature, as shown below.
